{"name":"Axe Handle","hex":"#6b4730","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"axe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Ayerrerenge."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tool for felling trees or chopping wood etc. consisting of a heavy  head flattened to a blade on one side, and a  handle attached to it.","An ancient weapon consisting of a  head that has one or two blades and a long handle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/axe"},{"term":"handle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The part of an object which is (designed to be) held in the hand when used or moved.","An instrument for effecting a purpose (either literally or figuratively); a tool, or an opportunity or pretext."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To touch; to feel or hold with the hand(s).","To accustom to the hand; to take care of with the hands."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/handle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Axe","blocks":[{"text":"An axe is an implement that has been used for thousands of years to shape, split, and cut wood, to harvest timber, and as a weapon. The axe has many forms and specialised uses but generally consists of a head with a sharpened blade attached to a handle."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Felling_axe.jpg/330px-Felling_axe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Axe","wikidata":"Q39397"},{"title":"Handle","blocks":[{"text":"A handle is a part of, or an attachment to, an object that allows it to be grasped and manipulated by hand. The design of each type of handle involves substantial ergonomic issues, even where these are dealt with intuitively or by following tradition. Handles for tools are an important part of their function, enabling the user to exploit the tools to maximum effect. Package handles allow for convenient carrying of packages."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Tsuka.JPG/330px-Tsuka.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Handle","wikidata":"Q200266"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Felling_axe.jpg/500px-Felling_axe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Felling_axe.jpg/1280px-Felling_axe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Felling_axe.jpg/500px-Felling_axe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Double- and single-bit felling axesA diagram showing the main points on an axe","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFelling_axe.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Kokerbijl_van_het_Plainseautype_in_brons%2C_925_tot_800_VC%2C_vindplaats-_Maaseik%2C_Heppeneert%2C_Wayerveld%2C_collectie_Gallo-Romeins_Museum_Tongeren%2C_He_1.jpg/500px-Kokerbijl_van_het_Plainseautype_in_brons%2C_925_tot_800_VC%2C_vindplaats-_Maaseik%2C_Heppeneert%2C_Wayerveld%2C_collectie_Gallo-Romeins_Museum_Tongeren%2C_He_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Kokerbijl_van_het_Plainseautype_in_brons%2C_925_tot_800_VC%2C_vindplaats-_Maaseik%2C_Heppeneert%2C_Wayerveld%2C_collectie_Gallo-Romeins_Museum_Tongeren%2C_He_1.jpg/1280px-Kokerbijl_van_het_Plainseautype_in_brons%2C_925_tot_800_VC%2C_vindplaats-_Maaseik%2C_Heppeneert%2C_Wayerveld%2C_collectie_Gallo-Romeins_Museum_Tongeren%2C_He_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Kokerbijl_van_het_Plainseautype_in_brons%2C_925_tot_800_VC%2C_vindplaats-_Maaseik%2C_Heppeneert%2C_Wayerveld%2